Phishing is the practice of using deceptive methods to obtain sensitive information, such as social security numbers, bank account details and credit card numbers, from people online. It is a serious security threat that can result in identity theft and financial loss. To avoid becoming a victim of phishing, it's important to be aware of the common tactics used by scammers and to use caution when giving out personal information online. It's also important to keep your software up-to-date and use strong passwords for all accounts. Additionally, be wary of unsolicited emails and links asking for personal information; always double-check the sender’s identity before clicking on anything. Finally, never share personal information such as your social security number or bank account details over email or through online forms without verifying the legitimacy of the request first.assistant

